From 7326673a204acf031c837ece17af030f73b9a495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Farhan <farhanabdm@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 08:18:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gi): custom weapons

Add custom weapons, imported from the `weapons` of a custom character
pack: their own base ATK and substat (with GO's growth curves), ascension
ATK, passive name and texts per refinement, and passive buffs with their
value at R1-R5 for the wielder, the party or the other party members,
optionally behind a toggle. Images come from an existing weapon of the
same type, or from image URLs.

The Add Weapon dialog gets a "Custom Weapon" button to import, edit
(name, images, rarity, ATK and substat at level 90, buffs) and delete
custom weapons. Deleting an equipped custom weapon is safe: the
database gives the character a default weapon after the reload.

The nanoka converter now also reads weapon JSON. Weapon buff presets in
tools/custom-characters/buffs/<id>.json can name a passive parameter
(`param`) instead of values; this adds Silverdawn (15517).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
